Interpretation:
The pressure-portable rescuers40/45 from the F-state do transfer into the original replicate8 basin, but only from level10 upward. Cell41 shows the complementary pattern: it rescues only the low-pressure levels8..9. Therefore rescue identity undergoes a pressure-dependent handoff rather than having one universally portable single-cell repair.

Plain speak:
